    Carter driving on non-planar terrain. States: pose T_k (SE3StateBatch; x forward, z up), wheel speeds (VectorStateBatch2), pose T_{k+1}. Residual: rows 2..5 (yaw, forward, lateral, vertical) of Log((T_k Exp(dt_k xi))^-1 T_{k+1}) with xi = [0, 0, omega, v, 0, 0]; roll and pitch are left to terrain factors. Analytic Jacobians.

    Parameters
    ----------
    time_steps : DevicePointer
        Device buffer of ``capacity`` step durations [s].
    wheel_radius, track_width : float
        r and b [m].
    capacity : int
        Number of factors (steps) the buffer holds.

    SE3DifferentialDriveFactorBatch (factor)
      residual: dynamics residual (see docs/sphinx/dynamics.rst)
      time_steps: 1 float per factor
      relative: yes (needs an anchor: a constant state or a prior)
      use: Differential drive on non-planar terrain.
      notes: Prefer pycunls.mpc, which wires these for you.
      capacity: how many factors (or states) the arrays hold. Batches start with 0 active items: call set_num_active_factors(n) / set_num_active_states(n) before solving. Arrays are float32 GPU arrays (CuPy), C-contiguous.
    """

    def __init__(self, time_steps: object, wheel_radius: float, track_width: float, capacity: int) -> None: ...

